@startuml
title P2 Air Rooms - Coordinator Boundaries

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

actor "Pulsar app" as App
actor "Telegram bot" as Bot

rectangle "Coordinator control plane" {
  [Air lifecycle API] as API
  [Approach alias handlers] as Alias
  [Air policy service] as Policy
  [Air runtime resolver] as Resolver
}

rectangle "Coordinator runtime" {
  [Air session owner\n(stateFor / orderAir)] as Runtime
  [Personal orbit sessions] as Personal
  [Transmission + track schedulers] as Delivery
}

database "Store" {
  [airs] as Airs
  [air_members] as Members
  [air_invites + policies] as Invites
  [links (legacy)] as Links
}

App --> API : create / invite / join /\nconfirm / leave / dissolve
Bot --> Alias : /approach /accept /\n/decline /apart
Alias --> API : compatibility mapping
API --> Policy : authorize lifecycle + actions
API --> Airs : persist air state
API --> Members : persist membership state
API --> Invites : persist invite + policy rows
API --> Resolver : activate / park / dissolve
Alias --> Links : read legacy rows during migration

Resolver --> Airs : resolve active air by orbit
Resolver --> Members : build peer set\nand active membership
Resolver --> Links : backfill active links\ninto two-member Airs
Resolver --> Runtime : own shared session by air_id
Resolver --> Personal : park / restore orbit state

Delivery --> Resolver : current_air routing\nand shared ownership
Runtime --> Delivery : one FIFO / queue per air_id

note bottom of Resolver
  Rules enforced here:
  - one active Air per barycenter
  - no transitive link-chain delivery
  - living-air catch-up survives the move from link ids to air ids
  - leave detaches one barycenter without stopping the others
end note

@enduml
